{"packet_id":"D032-03","doc_id":"D032","jurisdiction":"Hoboken, NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Hoboken rent control base-rent freeze","requirement":"A landlord may not charge rent above what the landlord was receiving on the chapter's effective date, nor above the rent received on January 11, 1973 where that exceeds the rent authorized by this chapter.","key_value":"rents capped at those received on the chapter's effective date and on January 11, 1973","coverage_conditions":"Dwellings subject to Chapter 155 of the Hoboken City Code; no building age, size or owner limits are stated in this section.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Violation of Chapter 155 is punishable under N.J.S.A. 40:49-5, including a fine not exceeding $2,000; each dwelling unit is a separate violation.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Hoboken Mun. Code §155-25","quoted_span":"No landlord shall, after the effective date of this chapter, charge any rents in excess of what he was receiving from the effective date of this chapter; nor shall such landlord charge any rents in excess of what he was receiving on January 11, 1973, if such excess is in excess of the rental which is authorized by this chapter.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D032-03","doc_id":"D032","jurisdiction":"Hoboken, NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Hoboken vacancy decontrol increase cap","requirement":"On a tenant's voluntary vacancy of a registered apartment, the unit is decontrolled for the new tenant's initial rent, capped at a 25% increase over the last rent paid, excluding any capital improvement surcharge; decontrol is limited to once every three years.","key_value":"25% over last rent; decontrol at most once per 3 years","coverage_conditions":"Rental apartment units registered under §155-30 that are covered by Chapter 155; decontrol requires voluntary vacancy without harassment, duress or pressure, or a legal eviction or court order.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Decontrol is not available where the court order dispossesses a tenant for holding over after the lease term.","coverage_quotes":["The landlord shall be entitled to decontrol the apartment unit under this article only under the following circumstances"]},"exemptions":"The decontrolled apartment unit is exempt from Chapter 155 for the new tenant's initial rental only.","penalty":"The Board may rescind an improper decontrol, revert the rent, and prosecute the landlord under §155-21 (fine up to $2,000).","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Hoboken Mun. Code §155-31","quoted_span":"provided, however, that said rental shall be limited to an increase of 25% over the last rental paid by the tenant who voluntarily vacated the rental unit, exclusive of any capital improvement surcharge that is a component of said last rental.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
